2026-09-02: THE INDEX CONFLICTED THREE TIMES IN ONE DAY. ONE git config STOPS IT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`instructions/00_INDEX.txt` conflicted on three separate `git pull`s today,
and every time the resolution was the same: run the generator. The file is
built by `tools/build_instruction_index.py` FROM THE FOLDERS, so the two
sides of any merge are two renderings of state git has already merged
correctly in `instructions/open/` and `instructions/done/`. Picking between
those renderings by hand is the only resolution that can be wrong without
anyone noticing -- it silently drops one session's closure from the list
while both files are on disk.

`.gitattributes` now says the file takes a merge driver. GIT DOES NOT HONOUR
A DRIVER DEFINED IN A COMMITTED FILE -- deliberately, because a driver is
arbitrary code -- so each clone installs it once:

    git config merge.spacr-index.name \
        "rebuild instructions/00_INDEX.txt from the folders"
    git config merge.spacr-index.driver \
        'sh -c "python tools/build_instruction_index.py >/dev/null 2>&1 && \
                cp instructions/00_INDEX.txt \"\$1\"" -- %A'

CODEX: run those two lines in /mnt/firecuda2/codex/repo/spacr. Until you do,
the file will still conflict on your side and the fix on your side is the
same one it always was -- regenerate, `git add`, continue.

Without the driver installed, a merge falls back to the ordinary text merge,
which is what happens today: nothing breaks, it just conflicts. Keep
regenerating rather than editing by hand either way; the header of the index
says the same thing and it went nine days stale once.

