2026-09-06, HOME SESSION — I NEARLY DUPLICATED active_learning TOO
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Second time in two days, same mechanism, caught earlier this time because I
had just written the rule down.

Building 379's Suggest engine I wrote feature-building and model-fitting from
the annotation column -- and `spacr/active_learning.py` already has both.
`round_features` builds the measurement matrix per crop, for the same stated
reason I would have given. `retrain_round` fits on every label, scores on a
GROUPED held-out split so the accuracy is not an artefact of 190 labels from
one well, and writes per-class probabilities into `png_list`. It is better
than what I wrote: I was downsampling to balance classes; it holds out by
well.

`suggest.py` is now a thin layer that READS those probabilities. What is
genuinely new is only the storage discipline -- a suggested 1 stored as 11, a
write that carries IS NULL, and bulk keep/throw. An unscored database is told
to press Retrain rather than being handed a second model's opinion, because
two models would give the reviewer and the queue different answers with no way
to tell which was right.

WHAT CAUGHT IT: grepping the package before building, which is the rule from
the scorecard entry above. It cost one command and saved a duplicate. The rule
holds; I just have to apply it before writing rather than after.

