2026-09-08 — AND A SECOND CLAUSE: DERIVED STATE OUTLIVES THE PATCH THAT MADE IT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The rule above says a test that changes a global owns putting it back. The home
session found the case it does NOT cover, and the remedy is different enough
that it belongs beside rather than inside it.

    tests/qt/test_scrim_solver.py + test_settings_column_never_black.py
    -> 24 failures, each file green alone

`test_scrim_solver` only uses `monkeypatch`, and pytest reverts every one of
those correctly. The mutation WAS put back. What was not put back is whatever
READ it while it was wrong and kept the answer -- a stylesheet computed under
a fake theme, a memoised palette, a cached layout.

  FIRST CLAUSE   did I restore what I changed?          remedy: a `finally`
  SECOND CLAUSE  did anything read it while it was      remedy: recompute or
                 wrong, and keep what it derived?               invalidate

A perfectly disciplined monkeypatch satisfies the first and can still fail the
second, which is why five clean instances of the first rule did not prevent
this one.

NOT REPRODUCIBLE ON THE WORK MACHINE, and that is recorded rather than
resolved: 61 passed at HEAD, at 05647692e^ and at fe50ff096. It is the sixth
machine-specific divergence this week, after the licence table (invisible under
old setuptools), the force-quit symptom (invisible offscreen), the ambient leak
(invisible until written to a real QSettings), the foreign path (visible ONLY
on the machine that has the data), and PySide6.QtPdf (unimportable on the home
box, fine here). Work machine: PySide6/Qt 6.11.1, Python 3.13.14, pytest 9.1.1.

THE STANDING LESSON, which is now earned six times over: a green result from
one machine is evidence about that machine. Neither session should close an
item on the other's inability to reproduce it, in either direction.
