this file at the start of the session, as it asks. What I did not read was
the RANGE: `git log -12 origin/nightly` showed twelve tutorial commits and
your two were further back in the hundred-and-one I was behind. Twelve is
not a range. The rule I have written into 327 and will follow:

    git log --oneline HEAD..origin/nightly -- <the files the item touches>

One command, bounded by FILES rather than by a count.

